{"explanation":"Replace manual random-byte AES key construction with an AES KeyGenerator-produced master key while preserving the existing PBKDF2-derived password wrapping input, constructor entry point, encrypted-record representation, and checked-exception contract. This does not alter persisted fields or their interpretation.","review_assumptions":["The coordinated EncryptedKey implementation continues to treat the first EncryptedKey.encrypt argument as the wrapping key and the second argument as the protected master key; retaining the PBKDF2-derived wrapping input is necessary for the existing decrypt(String) flow and persisted-record compatibility.","Supported Android providers continue to support AES KeyGenerator initialization at 256 bits, consistent with the previous 32-byte AES key size.","The broader provenance finding should be manually rechecked against EncryptedKey's Cipher.init argument after assembly: this file changes the generated protected master key's origin without changing the password-derived wrapping-key lifecycle required by the existing persisted format."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"medium","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/MasterKey.java","original_code":"import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.SecretKeyFactory;","edit_kind":"declaration","corrected_code":"import javax.crypto.KeyGenerator;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.SecretKeyFactory;","reason":"Import KeyGenerator so the protected AES master key is created by the AES provider rather than by manually assigning random bytes to a SecretKeySpec.","symbol":"javax.crypto imports"},{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/MasterKey.java","original_code":"    private MasterKey(PBEKeySpec spec) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException, BadPaddingException,
            NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeySpecException, IOException {
        SecretKeyFactory skf = getSecretKeyFactory();
        SecretKey pwd = skf.generateSecret(spec);

        byte[] raw = new byte[pwd.getEncoded().length];
        new SecureRandom().nextBytes(raw);
        SecretKey key = new SecretKeySpec(raw, "AES");

        mEncryptedKey = EncryptedKey.encrypt(pwd, key);
        mIterations = spec.getIterationCount();
        mAlgorithm = skf.getAlgorithm();
        mSalt = spec.getSalt();
    }","edit_kind":"method","corrected_code":"    private MasterKey(PBEKeySpec spec) throws NoSuchAlgorithmException,
            IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException, BadPaddingException,
            NoSuchPaddingException, InvalidKeySpecException, IOException {
        SecretKeyFactory skf = getSecretKeyFactory();
        SecretKey pwd = skf.generateSecret(spec);

        KeyGenerator keyGenerator = KeyGenerator.getInstance("AES");
        keyGenerator.init(BYTES * 8);
        SecretKey key = keyGenerator.generateKey();

        mEncryptedKey = EncryptedKey.encrypt(pwd, key);
        mIterations = spec.getIterationCount();
        mAlgorithm = skf.getAlgorithm();
        mSalt = spec.getSalt();
    }","reason":"Generate the AES master key through KeyGenerator at the existing 256-bit size before supplying it to EncryptedKey.encrypt. The PBKDF2 result remains the wrapping input so decrypt(String) continues to reproduce the key needed to decrypt existing encrypted records.","symbol":"MasterKey(PBEKeySpec)"}],"manual_review_required":true,"provided_contracts":["MasterKey retains its existing constructor and public generate(String) and decrypt(String) entry points, checked exceptions, PBKDF2 metadata, and persisted encrypted-key representation.","The AES master key protected by EncryptedKey.encrypt is generated by an AES KeyGenerator initialized to the existing 256-bit key size.","MasterKey continues to invoke EncryptedKey.encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey) with the existing argument order and remains compatible with the coordinated unchanged caller-facing EncryptedKey API."],"required_contracts":["EncryptedKey.encrypt must retain its public name, parameter order, return type, and checked-exception contract.","EncryptedKey must retain the existing representation needed to decrypt records using the PBKDF2-derived wrapping key and stored PBKDF2 algorithm, salt, and iteration metadata.","Coordinated MasterKey tests must retain existing observable encryption/decryption assertions and verify the unchanged MasterKey entry point after AES KeyGenerator key creation."],"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/MasterKey.java","required_tests":["Run the edited MasterKey instrumentation test to verify MasterKey.generate(String) and decrypt(String) retain their existing observable round-trip behavior.","Run EncryptedKey and AndroidKeyStore instrumentation tests with the coordinated explicit-GCM parameter implementation.","Compile the mobile module and androidTest sources on supported Android providers, confirming 256-bit AES KeyGenerator support and retained-record decryption."]}
